From 7d490d3ce89f40e6c9e464c110b1fcf925c202c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:11:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Muse: playlists, counted listens, and adding to the queue

The library and its player, with nothing on screen yet:

- muselib: Playlists/*.m3u and .m3u8 are read as albums whose tracks
  live in other albums' folders, after everything else. A line resolves
  beside the playlist, from the card's top, or - for a path from another
  computer, a file:// URL included - from its Music or Audiobooks folder
  down, in any case; never to anything off the card. A line too long for
  any path on the card is passed over whole.
- musec: musec_on_played tells of a listen - thirty seconds of a track,
  or half of a short one, played forward, not sought past - the moment
  it is enough, once a listen; never for a book. musec_append adds to the
  queue without stopping what plays (songs are not put on the end of a
  book: they start), and musec_jump plays a track of the queue.
- musequeue: muq_append, after the current track or at the end of the
  order, what is queued keeping its place.

tools/muselib-check and tools/musequeue-check cover the playlist lines
and the appending.
